
---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const assets = '/images/digital-arithmetic-system';
---

<Layout title="8-bit Digital Arithmetic System — Tarik Agić">
  <main class="article">
    <a class="back" href="/work">← All projects</a>

    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Digital Logic <span>·</span> Academic Project <span>·</span> 2025
      </p>

      <h1>8-bit Digital Arithmetic System</h1>

      <p class="dek">
        A breadboard-built arithmetic system with two operand registers,
        selectable clock sources, an 8-bit ripple-carry adder, and an
        extended finite-state machine for formal verification.
      </p>

      <div class="byline">
        <span>Tarik Agić &amp; Salih Seferović</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Team project</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="body">
      <section aria-labelledby="overview">
        <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>

        <p>
          Designed and implemented as a physical digital-logic project,
          this system stores two unsigned 8-bit operands, A and B, in
          separate registers. Either operand can be incremented using a
          shared arithmetic circuit, while a separate combinational
          ripple-carry adder continuously computes their sum.
        </p>

        <p>
          The project combines discrete logic hardware with a formal
          description of its sequential behavior. It addresses both
          the arithmetic correctness of the circuit and the control
          rules that determine which register changes on a clock event.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="hardware" class="clearfix">
        <h2 id="hardware">Hardware Implementation</h2>

        <figure class="article-image article-image--right">
          <a
            href={`${assets}/prototype.jpg`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            aria-label="Open photograph of the physical prototype"
          >
            <img
              src={`${assets}/prototype.jpg`}
              alt="Top-down photograph of the assembled 8-bit digital arithmetic system on multiple breadboards"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>

          <figcaption>
            <strong>Figure 1.</strong> Physical breadboard implementation.
            Click to enlarge.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          The prototype was assembled across six solderless breadboards
          using 74HC-series logic ICs. Two SN74HC273 registers hold the
          operands, and SN74HC157 multiplexers select the operand passed
          through a shared incrementer. A register-selection switch
          routes valid clock events to only the chosen register.
        </p>

        <p>
          Users can select a debounced push-button clock or an adjustable
          NE555 oscillator. The output stage uses LEDs to indicate the
          sum and carry; shift registers also support serial transfer
          to an Arduino-driven LCD for decimal display.
        </p>

        <figure class="architecture-figure">
          <a
            href={`${assets}/architecture.png`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            aria-label="Open system architecture diagram in full resolution"
          >
            <img
              src={`${assets}/architecture.png`}
              alt="System architecture showing clock sources, register selection, shared incrementer, ripple-carry adder, and output stage"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>

          <figcaption>
            <strong>Figure 2.</strong> System architecture: control signals,
            registers, arithmetic paths, and output stage.
            Click to enlarge.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="verification">
        <h2 id="verification">Formal Modeling and Verification</h2>

        <p>
          The sequential behavior was specified as an
          <strong>extended finite-state machine (EFSM)</strong>.
          Each state records the selected register, selected clock
          source, and both 8-bit operand values. An executable reference
          model was used to examine arithmetic correctness,
          register-update exclusivity, clock-source isolation,
          stability between valid events, and transition totality.
        </p>

        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <caption>Scope of the exhaustive formal-model checks</caption>

            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Measure</th>
                <th scope="col">Result</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>EFSM states</td>
                <td class="numeric">262,144</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Modeled event types</td>
                <td class="numeric">6</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>State-event transitions evaluated</td>
                <td class="numeric">1,572,864</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Assertion violations</td>
                <td class="numeric">0</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          The exhaustive checks establish these properties for the
          <em>formal model</em>; they do not constitute exhaustive
          electrical verification of the physical prototype.
          Physical tests were used separately to assess whether the
          assembled circuit behaved consistently with the model.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <span>
        Digital Logic · Sequential Circuits · EFSM · Formal Verification
      </span>

      <a href="/work">← Back to work</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article {
    width: min(820px, calc(100% - 48px));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 56px 0 96px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-flex;
    color: #9d9b97;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back:hover,
  .article a:hover {
    color: #f26a2e;
  }

  .article-header {
    padding: 56px 0 38px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #34312e;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 19px;
    color: #b3aaa1;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .eyebrow span {
    margin: 0 7px;
    color: #6f6a64;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 790px;
    margin: 0 0 21px;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.2vw, 3.45rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.047em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .dek {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 0;
    color: #bcb7b0;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .byline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 23px;
    color: #a5a09a;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .separator {
    color: #6c6863;
  }

  .body {
    padding-top: 5px;
  }

  .body section {
    margin-top: 34px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: #f1eee8;
    font-size: 1.34rem;
    font-weight: 550;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: #c2beb8;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .body strong {
    color: #e9e5df;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .body a {
    color: #e9e5df;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  /* Editorial image beside the text */

  .article-image {
    float: left;
    width: 38%;
    max-width: 300px;
    margin: 5px 25px 16px 0;
  }

  .article-image--right {
    float: right;
    margin: 5px 0 16px 25px;
  }

  .article-image a,
  .architecture-figure a {
    display: block;
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }

  .article-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid #38342f;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .article-image a:hover img,
  .architecture-figure a:hover img {
    border-color: #a49a8d;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 9px;
    color: #aaa49d;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  figcaption strong {
    color: #e5dfd7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* Architecture diagram */

  .architecture-figure {
    clear: both;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 26px auto 8px;
  }

  .architecture-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    background: #e9e7e2;
    border: 1px solid #38342f;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .clearfix::after {
    content: "";
    display: table;
    clear: both;
  }

  /* Results table */

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 22px 0 28px;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.83rem;
  }

  caption {
    padding: 0 0 12px;
    color: #a39e97;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: 12px 13px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #34312e;
    text-align: left;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  th {
    color: #aaa49c;
    font-weight: 500;
    background: #171614;
    border-top: 1px solid #34312e;
  }

  td {
    color: #ddd8d1;
  }

  tbody tr:hover {
    background: #171614;
  }

  .numeric {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Footer */

  .article-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 45px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid #34312e;
    color: #99948d;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .article-footer a {
    color: #ded8d0;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* Responsive layout */

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .article {
      width: calc(100% - 36px);
      padding-top: 35px;
    }

    .article-header {
      padding: 38px 0 30px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 9vw, 2.6rem);
    }

    .body section {
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .article-image,
    .article-image--right {
      float: none;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 340px;
      margin: 20px auto 22px;
    }

    .architecture-figure {
      width: 100%;
      margin: 22px auto;
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding: 10px 9px;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .back,
    .article-image img,
    .architecture-figure img {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
